"[2311.00962] Detecting Generated Images by Real Images Only (https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00962)\nciteturn1view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.00962\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 2 Nov 2023]\nL9: # Title:Detecting Generated Images by Real Images Only\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Xiuli Bi , cite6†Bo Liu , cite7†Fan Yang , cite8†Bin Xiao , cite9†Weisheng Li , cite10†Gao Huang , cite11†Pamela C. Cosman L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Detecting Generated Images by Real Images Only, by Xiuli Bi and Bo Liu and Fan Yang and Bin Xiao and Weisheng Li and Gao Huang and Pamela C. Cosman\nL14: \nL15: cite12†View PDF cite13†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:As deep learning technology continues to evolve, the images yielded by generative models are becoming more and more realistic, triggering people to question the authenticity of images. Existing generated image detection methods detect visual artifacts in generated images or learn discriminative features from both real and generated images by massive training. This learning paradigm will result in efficiency and generalization issues, making detection methods always lag behind generation methods.\nL17: This paper approaches the generated image detection problem from a new perspective: Start from real images. By finding the commonality of real images and mapping them to a dense subspace in feature space, the goal is that generated images, regardless of their generative model, are then projected outside the subspace. As a result, images from different generative models can be detected, solving some long-existing problems in the field.\nL18: Experimental results show that although our method was trained only by real images and uses 99.9\\% less training data than other deep learning-based methods, it can compete with state-of-the-art methods and shows excellent performance in detecting emerging generative models with high inference efficiency. Moreover, the proposed method shows robustness against various post-processing. These advantages allow the method to be used in real-world scenarios.\nL19: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite14†arXiv:2311.00962 [cs.CV]\nL21:    | (or cite15†arXiv:2311.00962v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL22:    | cite16†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2311.00962†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Xiuli Bi [cite17†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Thu, 2 Nov 2023 03:09:37 UTC (11,121 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Detecting Generated Images by Real Images Only, by Xiuli Bi and Bo Liu and Fan Yang and Bin Xiao and Weisheng Li and Gao Huang and Pamela C. Cosman\nL33: \nL34:   * cite12†View PDF L35:   * cite13†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite18†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite19†view license L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.CV\nL42: \nL43: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L44: \nL45: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2023-11 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite25†cs L50: \nL51: ### References & Citations\nL52: \nL53:   * cite26†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L54:   * cite27†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L55:   * cite28†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L56: \nL57: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL58: \nL59: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL60: \nL61: [Button: ×]\nL62: \nL63: loading...\nL64: \nL65: Data provided by:\nL66: \nL67: ### Bookmark\nL68: \nL69: [